PKGBUILD_PLAN_ADAPTER(3)

# NAME

pkgbuild_plan_adapter - project verified build artifacts into libpkgplan

# SYNOPSIS

*#include <libpkgbuild-plan/adapter.h>*

# DESCRIPTION

*project_artifact* accepts a complete successful *build_result*, a transport
pathname, and a *pkgimage::archive_backend*.

The adapter verifies the transport byte count and exact SHA-256 against build
authority, inspects the archive through *libpkgimage*, and compares every
normalized image entry with the ordered build payload. Path, type, mode, numeric
ownership, size, timestamp, link data, device data, and regular-content digest
must match.

After verification, the adapter projects source-owned candidate control through
*libpkgsource-plan* and constructs a *pkgplan::artifact_package_fact*. The
planner manifest identity binds the build result, request, payload, candidate,
artifact bytes, normalized image, and inspection receipt.

The adapter does not resolve requirements, execute builds, or install packages.

# ERRORS

A *projection_error* reports whether rejection came from incomplete build
result, source projection, archive inspection, payload mismatch, or planner-fact
construction.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgbuild*(3), *pkgbuild_result*(3), *libpkgimage*(3), *libpkgplan*(3)
